  "notes": "USAGE:\nOne of the most common する-verbs in Japanese. Used both transitively ({問題|もんだい}を{解決|かいけつ}する — to solve a problem) and intransitively ({問題|もんだい}が{解決|かいけつ}する — the problem is resolved).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {問題|もんだい}を{解決|かいけつ}する (to solve a problem)\n- {解決|かいけつ}{策|さく} (solution, remedy)\n- {解決|かいけつ}に{向|む}けて (toward a resolution)\n- {根本的|こんぽんてき}な{解決|かいけつ} (fundamental resolution)\n- {解決|かいけつ}{済|ず}み (resolved, settled)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {解消|かいしょう}する: to eliminate, to dissolve — for getting rid of problems or stress\n- {片付|かたづ}ける: to deal with, to settle — more informal",
